+  ⚠ RECORDED THE SAME DAY BUT AFTER THE FACT, and that is itself the first defect of this task.
+  `contract.md` asserted these rulings were "recorded in escalations.log" while the log held
+  nothing. scope-auditor FAILed on exactly that and was right: a contract citing an authority
+  record that does not corroborate it is a self-certification wearing a citation. The words below
+  are verbatim from the conversation; nothing is reconstructed or paraphrased.
+
+  WHAT PROMPTED IT. The catalogue is declared the single source of every metric definition, and
+  NO MODEL READS IT — checked in the compiled manifest, only tests depend on the seed. Formulas
+  are hand-copied and nothing compares them: of 68 model expressions carrying a catalogue
+  metric_id, 20 match the catalogue formula literally and 48 differ. Most differences are benign
+  re-grounding (the formula is written at leg grain, the model composes pre-aggregated atoms) or
+  the player zero-fill the 2026-06-25 ruling requires. ONE is a real divergence:
+  `finishing_efficiency` clamps to NULL when goals-minus-penalties is negative or exceeds shots on
+  target, and the catalogue's formula columns say nothing about it.
+
+  CPO INSTRUCTION, verbatim: "add the missing team totals and the count metrics to the catalogue."
+  Measured cause: classifying all 80 rows by formula shape, the PLAYER side carries 28 plain
+  totals (`sum(x)`, no denominator) and the TEAM side carries 4. The team surface is 15 per-match
+  rates and 7 ratios, so team quantities the product displays had no row to point at.
+
+  ⭐ CPO RULING 1, verbatim: "win, draw, loss are not metrics. they are results of a match."
+  W/D/L is a categorical attribute of a match, already carried by `result`; counting it tallies a
+  dimension rather than measuring anything. THREE drafted rows dropped. That removed the entire
+  cascade they had caused: the generator emitted `wins`/`draws`/`losses` blocks that COLLIDED with
+  hand-written ones and made `dbt parse` fail outright; without the rows there is no collision, no
+  `standings_wins/draws/losses` rename, no 6 repoints, `shared_columns.md` untouched, 16 files to
+  14. It also dissolved the defect that had FAILED the previous review round in two places — a
+  `draws` direction listed as an open question and shipped as a concrete value anyway.
+
+  ⭐ CPO RULING 2, verbatim: "use clean_sheets (for the number of matches with clean sheets) and
+  clean_sheets_share (for the percentage of matches with clean sheets)."
+  This RENAMES a metric that already ships, so it is its own MR, not part of this one. It resolves
+  a live two-meanings defect rather than working around it: `mart_team_profile.clean_sheets` is a
